# Workshop NCB (Eurosystem) root certificate.
#
# Trust anchor for verifying offline DE tokens (`de-offline+jwt`) per
# ADR 0010 §1. Self-signed P-256 root, 10-year validity,
# CN=Accesa Workshop NCB Offline Root. The NCB-issuer signs each
# token's leaf cert under this root and embeds `x5c = [leaf, root]`
# in the JWS header; the wallet PKIX-validates the leaf back to this
# anchor and ES256-verifies the JWS against the leaf's public key.
#
# Canonical source (companion repo):
#   services/ncb-issuer/src/main/resources/workshop-root/cert.pem
#
# Rotation: this anchor is intentionally stable. The NCB leaf rotates
# at every pod restart (fresh keypair per start, same root signs the
# new leaf) — historical tokens still verify because their JWS embeds
# the leaf that signed them. Only re-bundle when key.pem changes.
#
# NB: this trust hierarchy is INTENTIONALLY DISTINCT from the ECB-rooted
# /ncb/cert-chain hierarchy (ADR 0003). That chain regenerates on every
# cluster reset and is wrong for a bearer instrument the wallet holds
# for weeks. ADR 0010 §1 documents the rationale.
